## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical firewall configuration skills on RHEL 9, requiring precise rule creation, persistence, and verification—essential for enterprise security administration.

## Key Concepts
- nftables ruleset syntax and packet flow
- Rule persistence via /etc/nftables.conf
- Service management with systemctl
- Connectivity testing from allowed vs. disallowed sources
- Verification using nft list ruleset

## Code Example
```bash
#!/usr/sbin/nft -f
flush ruleset
table inet filter {
  chain input {
    type filter hook input priority 0; policy drop;
    iifname "lo" accept
    ip saddr 192.168.1.0/24 tcp dport 22 accept
  }
  chain forward {
    type filter hook forward priority 0; policy drop;
  }
  chain output {
    type filter hook output priority 0; policy accept;
  }
}
```

## Implementation Steps
```bash
# Install nftables
dnf install -y nftables

# Create ruleset
cat > /etc/nftables.conf << 'EOF'
#!/usr/sbin/nft -f
flush ruleset
table inet filter {
  chain input {
    type filter hook input priority 0; policy drop;
    iifname "lo" accept
    ip saddr 192.168.1.0/24 tcp dport 22 accept
  }
  chain forward {
    type filter hook forward priority 0; policy drop;
  }
  chain output {
    type filter hook output priority 0; policy accept;
  }
}
EOF

# Enable and start services
systemctl enable nftables
systemctl start nftables
systemctl status nftables

# Verify rules
nft list ruleset

# Test connectivity (from allowed host)
ssh user@server-ip

# Test connectivity (from disallowed host)
ssh user@server-ip  # Should timeout/refuse
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical mastery of containerized TLS termination, lifecycle upgrades, and host firewall controls in RH9.

## Key Concepts
- Podman/nginx-like TLS termination
- systemd drop-ins for zero-downtime reloads
- nftables rate limiting
- SELinux policy for container access
- certificate rotation with hot reload

## Code Example
```bash
# container run (example)
podman run -d --name proxy \
  -v /srv/certs:/etc/nginx/certs:ro \
  -p 8443:8443:Z nginx:latest
```

```bash
# systemd drop-in (ExecReload for zero downtime)
[Service]
ExecReload=/bin/kill -HUP $MAINPID
```

```bash
# minimal SELinux module (conceptual)
module proxytls 1.0;
require {
  type container_t;
  class file read; class tcp_socket name_bind; 
}
# allow container_t to read certs and bind 8443
allow container_t cert_dir_t:file read;
allow container_t self:tcp_socket name_bind;
```

```bash
# nftables (inbound 8443 and global rate limit)
table inet proxy {
  chain input {
    type filter hook input priority 0;
    tcp dport 8443 accept
  }
}
table inet limit {
  chain input {
    type filter hook input priority 0;
    limit rate 100/minutediffers
  }
}
```

